       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 200 mg/day. Higher doses add risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI or bleeding effects, and they haven't been shown to work better. Your patient's normal renal and hepatic function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nCould this be a typo? Here are some common intended doses:\n- **50 mg daily:** the usual starting dose for depression, GAD, and similar conditions.\n- **100 mg daily:** a typical titration step.\n- **200 mg daily:** the maximum.\n- **25 mg daily:** a lower starting dose, often used for panic disorder or PTSD.\n\nIf you do want 400 mg, for example on a psychiatry recommendation, tell me and add a note with the rationale. I can enter it with that note, though pharmacy will probably want to verify it. Otherwise, tell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
